This branch generates a structured quadrilateral mesh in a concentric annulus.

Configure the geometry and resolution in params.h. The computational-domain
edges, radial-layer mapping and element topology are defined in edgefunctions.h.
mesh.cpp contains the mesh-generation workflow. Then run:

    ./make.sh

The default output is ring.xml. To use another output name:

    ./make.sh my-ring.xml

Boundary composites in the generated Nektar++ XML are:

    C[0]  inner circle
    C[1]  outer circle

radialGrowth controls radial spacing. A value of 1 gives uniform spacing; a
value greater than 1 clusters cells near the inner circle.
